{
  "source": "ban-shallow-heavy-scan (GROUP L). Heavy recursive scans at depth <= 2 saturate / (99% full). du -xh -d1 / timed out at 300s (BHD-209).",
  "rule_ids": {
    "scan": "block-shallow-heavy-scan"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Deny class: heavy scan program (find/du/rg/fd/rgrep always-heavy; grep/egrep -r; ls -R; eza -T without -L) targeting an absolute path at depth <= 2 (/ , /x , /x/y).",
    "Depth >= 3 is allowed (LD4: du at depth 3). eza -T -L N stays allowed (discovery step, LD2).",
    "rg/fd/rgrep are recursive by DEFAULT — no flag gate (gotcha G5.2).",
    "pattern-first programs (rg/fd/grep/egrep/rgrep) skip the first non-flag arg (the pattern) before path extraction (gotcha G4.6).",
    "Path normalized: // collapsed, trailing / dropped, . skipped, .. pops (gotcha G5.1).",
    "Raw fallback matches ~/$HOME/${HOME} (shell-quote expands them to empty arg).",
    "find/grep/egrep home-prefix paths defer to GROUP K (block-home-wide-find/grep) to avoid double-deny (gotcha G4.8).",
    "Fail-open stays default (source must be opa, never fail-open). Unlock per-rule (block-shallow-heavy-scan), no god-key."
  ],
  "cases": [
    { "id": "du-root", "command": "du -sh /", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "root depth 0." },
    { "id": "du-var", "command": "du -sh /var", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "depth 1. Hung 300s in investigation." },
    { "id": "du-home", "command": "du -sh /home", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "depth 1. Hung 300s in investigation." },
    { "id": "du-home-bhd", "command": "du -sh /home/bhd", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "depth 2." },
    { "id": "du-var-lib", "command": "du -sh /var/lib", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "depth 2." },
    { "id": "find-root", "command": "find /", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "find root." },
    { "id": "find-usr", "command": "find /usr", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "depth 1, not home (GROUP K does not cover /usr)." },
    { "id": "rg-var", "command": "rg foo /var", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "rg recursive-by-default, pattern foo, path /var." },
    { "id": "fd-home", "command": "fd foo /home", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "fd recursive-by-default." },
    { "id": "grep-r-root", "command": "grep -r foo /", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "flag-gated grep, recursive." },
    { "id": "ls-R-root", "command": "ls -R /", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "flag-gated ls, -R." },
    { "id": "rgrep-root", "command": "rgrep foo /", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "rgrep is recursive by name." },
    { "id": "du-dollar-home", "command": "du -sh $HOME", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "raw $HOME token (shell-quote expands to empty arg)." },
    { "id": "du-tilde", "command": "du -sh ~", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "raw ~ token." },
    { "id": "eza-tree-root", "command": "eza -T /", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": "eza unbounded tree (no -L)." },
    { "id": "du-dotdot", "command": "du -sh /var/lib/..", "expect": "deny", "rule_id": "block-shallow-heavy-scan", "notes": ".. normalization: /var/lib/.. resolves to /var (depth 1)." },

    { "id": "du-depth3", "command": "du -sh /var/lib/docker", "expect": "allow", "notes": "LD4: du allowed at depth 3." },
    { "id": "find-depth4", "command": "find /var/lib/docker/overlay2", "expect": "allow", "notes": "depth 4 allowed." },
    { "id": "rg-depth3", "command": "rg foo /var/lib/docker", "expect": "allow", "notes": "depth 3 allowed." },
    { "id": "du-home-local", "command": "du -sh /home/bhd/.local", "expect": "allow", "notes": "depth 3 allowed (LD4)." },
    { "id": "eza-level2", "command": "eza -T -L 2 /", "expect": "allow", "notes": "eza bounded discovery step (LD2)." },
    { "id": "find-dot", "command": "find .", "expect": "allow", "notes": "cwd-relative." },
    { "id": "du-dot", "command": "du -sh .", "expect": "allow", "notes": "cwd-relative." },
    { "id": "fd-var-pattern", "command": "fd /var", "expect": "allow", "notes": "/var is the fd PATTERN, not path (gotcha G4.6)." },
    { "id": "grep-r-dot", "command": "grep -r foo .", "expect": "allow", "notes": "cwd-relative recursive." },
    { "id": "ls-etc", "command": "ls /etc", "expect": "allow", "notes": "ls non-recursive shallow." },
    { "id": "du-goals", "command": "du -sh ~/.pi/goals", "expect": "allow", "notes": "known goal dir (depth 3, raw ~ exempted)." }
  ]
}
